##:
net/error -- NetError, the error vocabulary of the net modules.

`NetError` is a predefined enum: the compiler synthesizes it, and this module is its
HOME (#574). The import is what brings the bare name into a unit, as `<io/fs>` brings
`FileMode`, and `use <net/error> as ne` puts it behind the dot (`ne.NetError.TimedOut`).
Every net module answers it -- `connect`, `bind`, `resolve`, `parse_ip` -- so a unit that
matches on one of their errors imports this module beside the one it calls.

The variant ORDER is the ABI: the index is the tag the socket layer stores into a Result
payload, so a variant is only ever appended.
:##

use <io/contracts>

##:
Turns a socket error into the one channel the io contracts answer.

Every NetError variant with no twin in IoError belongs to a connect, a bind or a resolve,
so nothing a contract method can answer is lost here. A stream that is already connected
cannot report AddressInUse.

- Returns: The IoError that says the same thing.
:##
extend NetError to_io() IoError:
    match self:
        NetError.ConnectionReset -> return IoError.ConnectionReset
        NetError.TimedOut -> return IoError.TimedOut
        NetError.Closed -> return IoError.Closed
        NetError.PermissionDenied -> return IoError.PermissionDenied
        NetError.TooManyOpen -> return IoError.TooManyOpen
        NetError.InvalidAddress -> return IoError.InvalidInput
        NetError.Interrupted -> return IoError.Interrupted
        _ -> return IoError.Other
